      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "AXIRIS look - DLSS 5 Neural Rendering (Merserk v9 engine, MIT)\n\nOne pass. Every slider is editable here: this workflow is made to be tuned by hand.\n\nTWO SETTINGS DESERVE ATTENTION, because their neutral-looking default does nothing:\n  . skin_structure = -1 does NOT mean \"minimum\". It means \"left to the engine\", and the\n    engine tends to overwork skin. Drive it instead (0 = no skin work, 2 = strong).\n  . tone_preservation keeps the SOURCE brightness. At 0 the render darkens; raise it until\n    the brightness comes back. It is a counterweight: too high and the effect fades.\n  . face_protection holds back the same work on faces.\n\nHOW TO JUDGE A SETTING: change ONE slider at a time, and read it twice - against the previous\nrender (what this slider changes) and against the source (whether the effect is still there).\n\nFOR DETAIL: upscale FIRST (it adds matter), then run DLSS 5."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "AXIRIS look - DLSS 5 Neural Rendering (Merserk v9 engine, MIT)\n\nOne pass. Every slider is editable here: this workflow is made to be tuned by hand.\n\nTWO SETTINGS DESERVE ATTENTION, because their neutral-looking default does nothing:\n  . skin_structure = -1 does NOT mean \"minimum\". It means \"left to the engine\", and the\n    engine tends to overwork skin. Drive it instead (0 = no skin work, 2 = strong).\n  . tone_preservation keeps the SOURCE brightness. At 0 the render darkens; raise it until\n    the brightness comes back. It is a counterweight: too high and the effect fades.\n  . face_protection holds back the same work on faces.\n\nHOW TO JUDGE A SETTING: change ONE slider at a time, and read it twice - against the previous\nrender (what this slider changes) and against the source (whether the effect is still there).\n\nFOR DETAIL: upscale FIRST (it adds matter), then run DLSS 5."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
